TITLE:: SDGSession
summary:: the whole mixer of a SuperDirtGUI saved under a name and brought back, VST plugin states included
categories:: Libraries>SuperDirtGUI
related:: Classes/SuperDirtGUI, Classes/SDGWindow, Classes/SDGInsert, Classes/SDGTrack

DESCRIPTION::
What a session in a DAW is, for the orbits: where everything stood. You use it
through the link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI:: or the top of the link::Classes/SDGWindow::;
it makes one of these itself, and you ask this class only about the folder and the names.

code::
~sdg.saveSession("gig");
~sdg.sessionNames;
~sdg.loadSession("gig", { |ok| ok.postln });
::

subsection:: What a session holds

table::
## strong::orbit:: || fader, mute, solo, limiter mode, output bus
## strong::tracks:: || which global effects, in what order, each one's fader, whether it is on, and what the knobs set
## strong::inserts:: || every insert of an orbit or a track, in its place, bypassed or not
## strong::eq, compressor:: || all of their settings; a compressor's sidechain too, by BusManager name when it has one
## strong::insight:: || what it shows and aims at
## strong::VST plugin:: || the plugin, and its state as the plugin hands it over
## strong::window:: || the tab and orbit on show, and the explorer's speed, amp and pan
::

It does not hold the content files, which are on disk already; sample banks,
which you load as you did; Tidal's patterns; or where the insert windows were.

A parameter is saved as the knobs set it, in the orbit's default event. A
value that only came in with a pattern is not: the pattern sends it again.

subsection:: On disk

A session is a folder in link::#*folder::, in the user's support directory so
that it outlives an update of the quark. In it are code::session.scd:: and one
code::.state:: file per VST insert. Copy the folder to give a session to someone;
a folder put there shows in the window's menu within a second.

The file code::session.scd:: is SuperCollider code, read by running it. strong::Load only
sessions you trust.::

subsection:: What loading does

It replaces what the orbits hold. Every insert is taken out and made again, each
plugin reopened with its state, so a plugin's sound stops for a moment. A track
whose effect is in the session stays and keeps ringing; the others go, and the
session's missing ones are added. Orbits beyond the session's are left as they are.

What cannot come back is left out with a warning, and the rest loads: an effect
with no SynthDef, an insert whose extension is not installed, a plugin that is
neither known by name nor on disk at its saved path. link::#-problems:: lists them.

A plugin saved by name opens through its saved file path when VSTPlugin has not
searched yet in this sclang, so a load needs no search on the machine that saved it.
Otherwise the search runs first, up to two minutes when it has never run.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: folder
Where sessions are kept. By default code::superdirt-gui-sessions:: in
code::Platform.userAppSupportDir::. Set it to keep them elsewhere.
ARGUMENT:: path
A folder; it is made at the first save.

METHOD:: names
The sessions in the folder, whatever the case.
RETURNS:: an Array of link::Classes/String::.

METHOD:: exists
ARGUMENT:: name
A session's name.
RETURNS:: whether there is a session of that name.

METHOD:: pathOf
ARGUMENT:: name
A session's name.
RETURNS:: its folder, whether or not it exists, as a link::Classes/String::.

METHOD:: nameProblem
Why a name will not do. It names a folder, on any system a student has.
ARGUMENT:: name
The name to try.
RETURNS:: a link::Classes/String::, or nil when the name will do.

METHOD:: version
RETURNS:: the version written into a session. One from a newer version loads
with a warning, and what is not known is left out.

METHOD:: new
Made by code::SuperDirtGUI:session::; you do not need to.
ARGUMENT:: sdg
Its link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI::.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: save
Ask each plugin for its state, at most five seconds in all, then write the session
over any of that name. A plugin that does not answer is saved with the state it
last gave. What would be written is read back first, and nothing is replaced if it
cannot be. Happens on AppClock: from a Routine of your own, wait for the action.
ARGUMENT:: argName
The name.
ARGUMENT:: action
Called with true, or false with a warning.

METHOD:: load
Replaces the mixer, as the description says. A session loaded in the same breath as
code::SuperDirtGUI(~dirt):: waits for the orbits to be ready, up to ten seconds.
ARGUMENT:: argName
The name.
ARGUMENT:: action
Called with true once every insert has its synth and every plugin its state, at
most thirty seconds on; with false and a warning when the session could not be read,
and then nothing was touched.

METHOD:: capture
The session as it would be written, on the clock the window's views allow: call it
on AppClock while the window is open.
RETURNS:: an link::Classes/Event::.

METHOD:: name
RETURNS:: the session saved or loaded last, nil before the first.

METHOD:: busy
RETURNS:: true during a save or a load. Another one meanwhile is refused with a warning.

METHOD:: problems
RETURNS:: what the last load left out, an Array of link::Classes/String::; empty when nothing.

METHOD:: windowState
The window's part of the last session, which a window opened later starts from.

METHOD:: sdg
RETURNS:: its link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI::.
